  data:  # b0c6
    kind: invariant  # b0c6
    title: "Swift field emission misclassifies function-local let/var as class-body fields"  # b0c6
    status: violated  # b0c6
    priority: 1  # b0c6
    parent: WI-jusus-zaron-donok-hidif-vabob-ruvak-tilik-zibid  # b0c6
    tags: []  # b0c6
    isbefore: []  # b0c6
    duplicate_of: []  # b0c6
    not_duplicate_of: []  # b0c6
    pr_ref:  # b0c6
    description: "WI-jusus's swift F5 slice (stored-property -> field) emits kind=\"field\" for ANY tree-sitter `property_declaration` that has an enclosing type. But local `let`/`var` bindings inside method/function bodies ALSO parse as `property_declaration` and have an enclosing type, so they leak in as fields. Invariant violated: an emitted swift field symbol must be a stored property declared DIRECTLY in a type body, never a function-local binding.\n\nBehavioral evidence (DEEP cohort deep-20260623-134237/cohort-001/iter-001, SwiftyJSON):\n- 383 of 407 emitted swift \"field\" nodes are in Tests/ files (XCTest method-body locals); only ~10 are genuine Source/ stored properties (JSON.rawArray, _type, _error, ...).\n- Repro: ArrayTests.swift:29 `let array = [\"1\",\"2\",\"a\",\"B\",\"D\"]` inside `func testSingleDimensionalArraysGetter()` of `class ArrayTests` -> emitted as field `ArrayTests.array`. Same for `let json`, ConcurrencyTests.swift:50 `let processor = Processor()`, PrintableTests.swift:103 `var debugDescription = ...`.\n\nRoot cause: classification keys off `_get_enclosing_type(node)` (nearest ancestor type) WITHOUT verifying the property_declaration is a DIRECT member of the type body (class_body / struct body) -- i.e. that no function_declaration / init_declaration / closure body sits between the node and the type. A local in a method has an enclosing type, so it is misclassified as that type's field.\n\nFix shape: in swift.py property_declaration handling, restrict the enclosing_type->field branch to declarations directly in the type body; reject when an intervening function / initializer / closure scope is found. Preserve the parent==source_file -> variable branch (audited 11/11 correct on this cohort). TDD: fixture with a method-local `let` inside a type asserting NO field node; expect SwiftyJSON 407 -> ~10 fields after fix; re-validate via bakeoff-deep cycle --workdir deep-20260623-134237 (iter-002).\n\nDiscovered by adversarial ground-truth audit (workflow f5-groundtruth-audit; swift REFUTED, 1/12 field samples correct). REGRESSION: shipped in this F5 session's swift slice (PR 2c821f17ad). Lab notebook: notebookjournal_06232026_1411.md."  # b0c6
    fields:  # b0c6
      statement: "An emitted swift field symbol must be a stored property declared directly in a type body, never a function-local let/var binding."  # b0c6
      root_cause: "swift.py field branch keys off _get_enclosing_type without checking the property_declaration is a direct member of the type body; method-local let/var (also parsed as property_declaration) inherit an enclosing type and leak in as fields."  # b0c6
